# Intergrax - session artifacts (no repo-root clutter)

**Never** create temporary, diagnostic, proof-run, or helper output files in the repository root or in tracked source trees.

## Required location

All such files go under **`.tmp/`** (gitignored). Use an existing subtree or create a scoped subfolder:

| Kind | Path |
|------|------|
| Platform / suite proof runs | `.tmp/proof/<suite-run-id>/` |
| Tool-scoped proof output | `.tmp/proof/<proof-id>/<run-id>/` |
| Agent session logs, repro captures, diag dumps | `.tmp/session/<topic-or-task-id>/` |
| One-off previews / scratch | `.tmp/session/scratch/` |

Examples (good):

```text
.tmp/session/WIN-DIAG-EMBEDDING-CLUSTER/ta-repro.log
.tmp/session/lkw-hosting-proof/pytest.log
.tmp/proof/lkw-trusted-ask-workspace-proof/run-2026-08-22.log
```

## Forbidden

- Dotfiles or logs at repo root (e.g. `.win-*.log`, `.diag-*.log`, `tee` to `./proof.log`)
- Redirecting proof/diag stdout into `applications/`, `agents/`, `intergrax/`, or `docs/`
- Leaving session artifacts in `sample_docs/`, `scripts/`, or other product paths unless the task explicitly commits that artifact

## Commands

When capturing shell output, always target `.tmp/`:

```powershell
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path .tmp/session/<task-id>
uv run ... 2>&1 | Tee-Object -FilePath .tmp/session/<task-id>/run.log
```

```bash
mkdir -p .tmp/session/<task-id>
uv run ... 2>&1 | tee .tmp/session/<task-id>/run.log
```

## Cleanup

Prefer writing only under `.tmp/`. Do not delete `.tmp/` wholesale unless the operator asks; subfolders are session-scoped and gitignored.
